{
  "id": "29396_kikakusuru",
  "headword": "{企画|きかく}する",
  "reading": "きかくする",
  "romaji": "kikakusuru",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to plan; to organize; to devise",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to plan; to organize; to devise",
      "explanation": "To plan and put together a project, event, or product — devising the concept and arranging how to realize it. Common in business and event contexts."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29396_kikakusuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "イベントを{企画|きかく}する。",
      "english": "to plan an event",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29396_kikakusuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{新|あたら}しい{商品|しょうひん}を{企画|きかく}している。",
      "english": "We are planning a new product.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29396_kikakusuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{社員|しゃいん}{旅行|りょこう}を{企画|きかく}することになり、{行|い}き{先|さき}を{考|かんが}えている。",
      "english": "I've been put in charge of organizing the company trip and am thinking about where to go.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: X を {企画|きかく}する (plan X).\n\nThe noun {企画|きかく} (\"a plan, a project\") and {企画|きかく}{書|しょ} (\"project proposal\") are very common in the workplace.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {企画|きかく}{書|しょ}: project proposal document\n- {企画|きかく}{部|ぶ}: planning department\n- イベントを{企画|きかく}する: to organize an event\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {計画|けいかく}する: to plan — focuses on the concrete schedule and steps; {企画|きかく} emphasizes devising the concept",
